  "description": "Decision 298's corner-reach probe for decision 294 (a) (phase1.25_pilot-wand item 2.7: whether a seam edge of another planar face, reached past its end at a UV corner of the island, reaches the ring texel within 1.0 texel when the seam edge meeting it there is gated, 1.15 otherwise, and decision 285's 1.78 when the two are collinear), exploratory: 432 copies of one island corner (two triangles at 1 texel per cm hinged 6 degrees, so that its two seam edges lie on different planar faces; their far islands are their own UV islands), the corner bent 90, 30, 10, 2, 1, 0.25, 0.05 and 0 degrees, the target ring texel beside the first edge at 0.90 to 1.30 texel from the corner, the first edge's far island folded 20 degrees concave (gated), 20 degrees convex (open, past the gate's dot product), 6 degrees convex (open) or absent (no seam), with and without covered texels, and the hinge 0 (one planar face), 2 and 20 degrees; each copy its own 3D piece, mesh box exactly [-256, 256] cm in x and z and [-64, 64] in y; document resolution 512. User0-User7 added as RGB32F (a record whose template capture shows one of them not 32F is void); one fill with the eight channels active, Normal at opacity 1, default projection (read back), sources the authored float32 kernel code at the document size: User0-User2 one-hot the nine classes x mod 3 + 3 (y mod 3) of the texel (column x, row y from the top), User3 the UV ramp R = (x + 0.5)/N, G = (y + 0.5)/N, B = 0.5, User4 and User5 the periodic codes d and e (k/256, one 17 x 13 texel tile each), User6 (d + e)/2 and User7 1 - d. The eight maps at OpenEXR 32f with infinite padding and with passthrough (every covered texel must equal its source bit for bit, or the probe is void), every export step done twice in the session.",
